1
00:01:32,610 --> 00:01:35,020
[Forging Justice]

2
00:01:35,210 --> 00:01:37,630
[Episode 23]

3
00:01:41,229 --> 00:01:41,560
It...

4
00:01:41,870 --> 00:01:43,800
It must be pretty jarring to hear me

5
00:01:43,920 --> 00:01:45,850
say all this out of the blue, right?

6
00:01:48,590 --> 00:01:49,000
I...

7
00:01:50,310 --> 00:01:52,110
just don't want to hold you back.

8
00:01:58,400 --> 00:01:59,200
I understand.

9
00:02:02,070 --> 00:02:02,760
And

10
00:02:03,200 --> 00:02:05,070
this isn't about holding anyone back—

11
00:02:05,070 --> 00:02:06,310
it's part of the process.

12
00:02:06,310 --> 00:02:07,510
You're in Beijing now

13
00:02:08,910 --> 00:02:11,170
and working with the law revision group.

14
00:02:12,000 --> 00:02:12,960
That's such a significant

15
00:02:12,960 --> 00:02:14,310
and meaningful undertaking.

16
00:02:14,310 --> 00:02:15,510
It's also your dream.

17
00:02:16,590 --> 00:02:17,000
I...

18
00:02:18,470 --> 00:02:19,490
wouldn't let you give all that up

19
00:02:19,490 --> 00:02:20,490
for me.

20
00:02:21,520 --> 00:02:22,150
And...

21
00:02:23,360 --> 00:02:25,890
it's hard for me
to be transferred to Beijing.

22
00:02:36,630 --> 00:02:37,310
The fact that you've thought about

23
00:02:37,310 --> 00:02:38,590
such practical things

24
00:02:39,870 --> 00:02:40,310
means

25
00:02:40,310 --> 00:02:41,030
you've seriously considered

26
00:02:41,030 --> 00:02:42,630
our future together, right?

27
00:02:48,150 --> 00:02:50,130
Just knowing that makes me very happy.

28
00:02:50,130 --> 00:02:51,380
Go back. I'm leaving.

29
00:03:06,280 --> 00:03:07,210
Wake up. Wake up.

30
00:03:07,360 --> 00:03:08,240
Tell us again—

31
00:03:08,630 --> 00:03:10,680
what time did you leave
Liu's house that day?

32
00:03:10,680 --> 00:03:12,010
I didn't check the time.

33
00:03:15,530 --> 00:03:16,840
After drinking with Liu,

34
00:03:16,840 --> 00:03:18,040
I went straight home.

35
00:03:21,190 --> 00:03:21,840
Man.

36
00:03:24,120 --> 00:03:25,030
Well, getting married

37
00:03:25,030 --> 00:03:26,710
really does change a guy, huh?

38
00:03:27,680 --> 00:03:28,280
Handsome.

39
00:03:32,630 --> 00:03:33,520
I look pretty decent, eh?

40
00:03:33,520 --> 00:03:34,120
Handsome.

41
00:03:34,870 --> 00:03:35,600
I haven't...

42
00:03:36,590 --> 00:03:38,050
even put on my tie yet.

43
00:03:38,230 --> 00:03:40,360
I'll look even better with it on. Look.

44
00:03:41,280 --> 00:03:42,140
Not bad, right?

45
00:03:43,710 --> 00:03:45,560
You didn't check the time
when you got home either?

46
00:03:45,560 --> 00:03:46,890
Sometime after 10 then.

47
00:03:47,190 --> 00:03:48,050
How much after?

48
00:03:49,430 --> 00:03:50,160
I don't know.

49
00:03:50,710 --> 00:03:52,240
I'm done drinking. No more.

50
00:03:52,310 --> 00:03:53,120
-No more.
-Done drinking?

51
00:03:53,120 --> 00:03:53,710
No more.

52
00:03:54,680 --> 00:03:55,590
Alright, then.

53
00:03:56,829 --> 00:03:57,680
I'm heading out.

54
00:03:57,680 --> 00:03:58,280
Go, go.

55
00:03:58,800 --> 00:03:59,400
Tomorrow morning,

56
00:03:59,400 --> 00:04:00,840
I still have to go into town
to pick up my brother.

57
00:04:00,840 --> 00:04:01,560
Go home, go.

58
00:04:01,800 --> 00:04:03,060
I'm heading home then.

59
00:04:03,430 --> 00:04:04,560
Get some rest early.

60
00:04:06,750 --> 00:04:07,870
You clean this up.

61
00:04:08,840 --> 00:04:09,430
Just go. Leave it to me.

62
00:04:09,430 --> 00:04:10,280
I'm off, off.

63
00:04:11,240 --> 00:04:11,910
Normally,

64
00:04:12,240 --> 00:04:13,700
how long does it take to get

65
00:04:13,840 --> 00:04:15,300
from Liu's house to yours?

66
00:04:16,160 --> 00:04:17,310
Over 20 minutes.

67
00:04:19,120 --> 00:04:20,380
And after you got home?

68
00:04:20,870 --> 00:04:21,730
I went to sleep.

69
00:04:22,240 --> 00:04:22,920
Went to sleep?

70
00:04:22,920 --> 00:04:24,870
You didn't turn on the lights first?

71
00:04:24,870 --> 00:04:26,530
I did, but they didn't come on.

72
00:04:27,680 --> 00:04:29,160
I guess there was a power outage.

73
00:04:29,160 --> 00:04:29,940
You're right.

74
00:04:29,940 --> 00:04:31,750
There was a power outage that night.

75
00:04:31,750 --> 00:04:33,430
But that was at 11:40.

76
00:04:33,830 --> 00:04:34,600
You said

77
00:04:34,600 --> 00:04:36,480
you left Liu's house a little after 10.

78
00:04:36,480 --> 00:04:38,120
Why did it take you
over an hour to get home?

79
00:04:38,120 --> 00:04:38,830
I just...

80
00:04:39,240 --> 00:04:40,070
What else could I have been doing?

81
00:04:40,070 --> 00:04:42,360
I went home.
What else would I have been doing?

82
00:04:42,360 --> 00:04:44,000
Why don't you just ask Liu?

83
00:04:44,830 --> 00:04:45,630
Tell us again—

84
00:04:45,630 --> 00:04:46,750
what happened to your hand,

85
00:04:46,750 --> 00:04:47,680
and how did the blood

86
00:04:47,680 --> 00:04:48,680
get on your shirt?

87
00:04:52,310 --> 00:04:53,570
What are you two doing?

88
00:04:54,360 --> 00:04:54,760
Hey...

89
00:04:55,360 --> 00:04:55,760
You...

90
00:04:56,120 --> 00:04:56,750
Hu Xudong,

91
00:04:57,430 --> 00:04:59,320
you need to understand
the situation you're in.

92
00:04:59,320 --> 00:05:00,040
Cooperating

93
00:05:00,040 --> 00:05:02,370
and coming clean is in your best interest.

94
00:05:04,120 --> 00:05:04,920
Captain Wang,

95
00:05:05,010 --> 00:05:06,010
come out for a sec.

96
00:05:08,630 --> 00:05:09,560
What's going on?

97
00:05:10,360 --> 00:05:11,490
We've got a witness.

98
00:05:12,360 --> 00:05:12,800
Who?

99
00:05:13,270 --> 00:05:15,070
A substation worker
getting off the evening shift.

100
00:05:15,070 --> 00:05:16,480
Around 11:10,

101
00:05:16,830 --> 00:05:18,240
he saw someone near the canal

102
00:05:18,240 --> 00:05:19,360
who looked like Yin Ping.

103
00:05:19,360 --> 00:05:20,390
Can he identify him for certain?

104
00:05:20,390 --> 00:05:21,390
He didn't get a clear look at the face,

105
00:05:21,390 --> 00:05:22,360
only the build.

106
00:05:22,720 --> 00:05:23,920
About 1.8 meters tall

107
00:05:23,920 --> 00:05:24,630
and fairly thin.

108
00:05:24,630 --> 00:05:25,830
Some features match.

109
00:05:30,630 --> 00:05:32,360
It takes about 20 minutes to get

110
00:05:32,560 --> 00:05:34,720
from the irrigation canal to the village.

111
00:05:34,720 --> 00:05:36,830
According to what Hu Xudong told us—

112
00:05:37,310 --> 00:05:38,920
he killed the victim and went home,

113
00:05:38,920 --> 00:05:40,780
and the power went out right then.

114
00:05:40,950 --> 00:05:42,610
That timing lines up exactly.

115
00:05:44,190 --> 00:05:45,320
Can we believe that?

116
00:05:47,820 --> 00:05:48,750
What did Liu, who was drinking with him,

117
00:05:48,750 --> 00:05:49,360
say?

118
00:05:50,580 --> 00:05:51,680
That guy was blackout drunk—

119
00:05:51,680 --> 00:05:53,600
he can't remember anything clearly.

120
00:05:53,600 --> 00:05:54,400
Captain Wang,

121
00:05:54,960 --> 00:05:56,760
does the timeline really add up?

122
00:05:58,480 --> 00:05:59,409
What's the rush?

123
00:06:00,360 --> 00:06:02,120
He definitely had the time
to commit the crime.

124
00:06:02,120 --> 00:06:04,180
It's his alibi that might not hold up.

125
00:06:04,480 --> 00:06:05,720
Well, does that mean...

126
00:06:05,720 --> 00:06:06,600
Mean what?

127
00:06:07,580 --> 00:06:08,130
Yin Ping

128
00:06:08,160 --> 00:06:09,830
was stabbed to death
with a triangular bayonet.

129
00:06:09,830 --> 00:06:11,120
That kind of wound is highly distinctive.

130
00:06:11,120 --> 00:06:12,000
Who else has that weapon

131
00:06:12,000 --> 00:06:13,200
in the whole village?

132
00:06:13,890 --> 00:06:15,690
That alone is enough to nail him.

133
00:06:15,810 --> 00:06:16,250
Yes.

134
00:06:17,430 --> 00:06:18,890
That bloodstained shirt—

135
00:06:19,270 --> 00:06:21,070
have the test results come back?

136
00:06:21,120 --> 00:06:22,000
The forensic examiner said

137
00:06:22,000 --> 00:06:23,360
the shirt was left soaking in a basin

138
00:06:23,360 --> 00:06:24,140
with other laundry

139
00:06:24,140 --> 00:06:24,900
for a while,

140
00:06:25,240 --> 00:06:26,510
so there could've been contamination.

141
00:06:26,510 --> 00:06:27,240
That's fine.

142
00:06:28,360 --> 00:06:29,680
As long as the blood on the shirt

143
00:06:29,680 --> 00:06:31,410
matches Yin Ping's blood type,

144
00:06:31,480 --> 00:06:33,340
the case is basically confirmed.

145
00:06:33,950 --> 00:06:34,680
Right? Look—

146
00:06:35,680 --> 00:06:36,800
we've got a motive,

147
00:06:37,480 --> 00:06:39,120
the opportunity, the murder weapon,

148
00:06:39,120 --> 00:06:39,890
and bloodstained shirt.

149
00:06:39,890 --> 00:06:41,690
We have all the evidence, right?

150
00:06:42,120 --> 00:06:42,630
Now all we need

151
00:06:42,630 --> 00:06:43,800
is his confession.

152
00:06:44,600 --> 00:06:45,950
Alright, I'll stop here.

153
00:06:45,950 --> 00:06:47,070
I'm going back to the interrogation.

154
00:06:47,070 --> 00:06:48,800
Got it. You've worked hard, Captain Wang.

155
00:06:48,800 --> 00:06:50,600
I'd like to see who cracks first.

156
00:06:55,430 --> 00:06:56,040
Judge Xia?

157
00:06:56,430 --> 00:06:57,040
Judge Xia!

158
00:06:59,750 --> 00:07:00,390
Coming.

159
00:07:01,360 --> 00:07:01,890
Who is it?

160
00:07:04,190 --> 00:07:05,250
What's the matter?

161
00:07:07,920 --> 00:07:09,800
You're the one who got Yin Ping killed!

162
00:07:09,800 --> 00:07:11,460
Get lost, you wretched woman!

163
00:07:22,310 --> 00:07:24,310
I'm all bandaged up like a mushroom.

164
00:07:25,070 --> 00:07:26,880
Actually, it's just a scrape.

165
00:07:27,160 --> 00:07:27,650
It's nothing serious.

166
00:07:27,650 --> 00:07:29,380
Just help me put a bandage on it.

167
00:07:32,360 --> 00:07:34,360
Look at those bastards.

168
00:07:35,310 --> 00:07:37,159
All they know is taking cheap shots.

169
00:07:37,159 --> 00:07:38,360
Ganging up on a woman?

170
00:07:38,630 --> 00:07:40,090
They're really scumbags.

171
00:07:40,600 --> 00:07:41,800
Stay with me tonight.

172
00:07:43,630 --> 00:07:45,240
I'll put up a fence for you tomorrow.

173
00:07:45,240 --> 00:07:47,300
Is a fence really going to solve this?

174
00:07:47,800 --> 00:07:49,040
They should be arrested for this.

175
00:07:49,040 --> 00:07:50,440
What the hell do you know?

176
00:07:50,680 --> 00:07:51,880
Now the whole village

177
00:07:51,950 --> 00:07:53,680
thinks Yin Ping died tragically.

178
00:07:53,680 --> 00:07:54,800
They're all targeting the Hu family

179
00:07:54,800 --> 00:07:55,390
and Xia.

180
00:07:55,720 --> 00:07:58,050
Wouldn't you just be making things worse?

181
00:08:08,160 --> 00:08:08,600
Qiao.

182
00:08:12,070 --> 00:08:12,870
Qiao Xiaojun.

183
00:08:16,360 --> 00:08:17,160
Don't run off.

184
00:08:18,480 --> 00:08:20,280
Why did you come to my workplace?

185
00:08:20,800 --> 00:08:21,630
This is what

186
00:08:22,120 --> 00:08:23,380
that female colleague

187
00:08:23,680 --> 00:08:24,510
brought for your child last time.

188
00:08:24,510 --> 00:08:26,070
She really likes your child.

189
00:08:26,070 --> 00:08:26,930
I don't want it.

190
00:08:29,720 --> 00:08:31,320
Swiss chocolate. Imported.

191
00:08:32,090 --> 00:08:33,419
Put it away, put it away.

192
00:08:34,549 --> 00:08:35,150
Come on.

193
00:08:36,150 --> 00:08:37,159
Take it. Take it.

194
00:08:37,760 --> 00:08:38,669
Someone asked me to do this.

195
00:08:38,669 --> 00:08:39,960
Just do me a favor and accept it, okay?

196
00:08:39,960 --> 00:08:40,600
Come on.

197
00:08:40,809 --> 00:08:41,740
Take it. Take it.

198
00:08:42,200 --> 00:08:42,870
Look, this is

199
00:08:42,870 --> 00:08:43,669
for Yan Jicai's daughter.

200
00:08:43,669 --> 00:08:45,130
I still have to deliver it.

201
00:08:47,150 --> 00:08:48,670
If you really don't want it,

202
00:08:48,670 --> 00:08:50,030
throw it away after I leave,

203
00:08:50,030 --> 00:08:50,390
okay?

204
00:08:51,120 --> 00:08:51,580
See you.

205
00:08:58,440 --> 00:08:59,500
Oh, one more thing.

206
00:08:59,720 --> 00:09:01,080
We didn't finish our conversation
at your place that day

207
00:09:01,080 --> 00:09:02,840
because your wife came back, right?

208
00:09:02,840 --> 00:09:03,600
Is there something

209
00:09:03,600 --> 00:09:05,060
you still haven't told us?

210
00:09:05,960 --> 00:09:06,550
No.

211
00:09:09,200 --> 00:09:10,360
My phone number

212
00:09:10,360 --> 00:09:11,080
and pager number are in there.

213
00:09:11,080 --> 00:09:12,790
I'll come find you another day.

214
00:09:12,790 --> 00:09:13,990
Or you can contact me.

215
00:09:14,840 --> 00:09:15,320
See you.

216
00:09:15,550 --> 00:09:16,080
Goodbye.

217
00:09:22,200 --> 00:09:24,610
[Nanlu Public Security Bureau]

218
00:09:24,640 --> 00:09:25,120
Come on.

219
00:09:25,750 --> 00:09:27,150
Come on, watch your rhythm!

220
00:09:27,150 --> 00:09:28,350
Footwork, footwork!

221
00:09:30,030 --> 00:09:31,490
Get in close, get in close!

222
00:09:31,840 --> 00:09:33,040
Where's your rhythm?

223
00:09:33,870 --> 00:09:34,510
Hit him!

224
00:09:35,550 --> 00:09:37,150
Go at him, go at him, go at him!

225
00:09:37,600 --> 00:09:39,020
Aggressive, be more aggressive!

226
00:09:39,020 --> 00:09:40,200
He's tired! Can't you tell?

227
00:09:40,200 --> 00:09:40,840
Hit him!

228
00:09:40,870 --> 00:09:41,790
Watch his left! Watch his left!

229
00:09:41,790 --> 00:09:42,990
Watch that left hook!

230
00:09:47,750 --> 00:09:48,440
Boss Ma!

231
00:09:48,630 --> 00:09:50,560
I'd be better off listening to him!

232
00:09:52,440 --> 00:09:53,770
We got him all confused.

233
00:09:54,270 --> 00:09:56,070
You're the one who threw him off.

234
00:09:58,320 --> 00:09:59,250
You have no tact.

235
00:10:08,080 --> 00:10:09,540
Back when you were a scout,

236
00:10:09,790 --> 00:10:11,000
didn't you learn some one-move takedowns?

237
00:10:11,000 --> 00:10:12,330
That really nasty kind.

238
00:10:13,270 --> 00:10:14,030
I didn't start learning boxing

239
00:10:14,030 --> 00:10:15,560
until after I came to Nanlu.

240
00:10:17,390 --> 00:10:18,790
Let's have a match later.

241
00:10:20,000 --> 00:10:21,170
How could I possibly beat you?

242
00:10:21,170 --> 00:10:22,720
I'm an amateur, all talk.

243
00:10:22,910 --> 00:10:24,120
I can't compare with you professionals.

244
00:10:24,120 --> 00:10:24,750
Why not?

245
00:10:25,240 --> 00:10:26,670
I think you're pretty good.

246
00:10:26,670 --> 00:10:27,380
To be honest,

247
00:10:27,380 --> 00:10:29,040
I might not be able to beat you.

248
00:10:30,440 --> 00:10:31,500
What's this about?

249
00:10:33,080 --> 00:10:33,870
Haven't seen you in a long time.

250
00:10:33,870 --> 00:10:34,550
I came to treat you to a meal.

251
00:10:34,550 --> 00:10:35,610
Don't give me that.

252
00:10:36,080 --> 00:10:37,140
I know you too well.

253
00:10:37,440 --> 00:10:38,870
You're the typical type—

254
00:10:39,960 --> 00:10:40,910
looking simple and honest

255
00:10:40,910 --> 00:10:42,550
but actually full of schemes.

256
00:10:42,550 --> 00:10:45,120
You've never bought me a meal
without wanting something.

257
00:10:45,120 --> 00:10:45,720
What is it?

258
00:10:46,320 --> 00:10:47,850
I really do need something.

259
00:10:48,870 --> 00:10:49,390
Well...

260
00:10:50,670 --> 00:10:52,000
Who was in charge of

261
00:10:52,030 --> 00:10:53,560
Yan Jicai's case back then?

262
00:10:54,870 --> 00:10:56,440
Why are you asking about that?

263
00:10:56,440 --> 00:10:57,570
Just asking around.

264
00:10:57,910 --> 00:11:00,170
Since when do you ever "just ask around"?

265
00:11:02,160 --> 00:11:03,080
I have a friend

266
00:11:03,150 --> 00:11:04,350
who works at a prison.

267
00:11:04,510 --> 00:11:05,980
He said Yan Jicai
has been claiming innocence

268
00:11:05,980 --> 00:11:07,080
the whole time over there—

269
00:11:07,080 --> 00:11:09,000
cutting his wrists,
going on hunger strikes, and all that.

270
00:11:09,000 --> 00:11:10,600
So he asked me to look into it.

271
00:11:11,080 --> 00:11:11,630
Have you ever seen

272
00:11:11,630 --> 00:11:13,390
a death row inmate
who doesn't claim innocence?

273
00:11:13,390 --> 00:11:13,850
Rarely.

274
00:11:16,120 --> 00:11:17,580
But he's asked many times,

275
00:11:17,720 --> 00:11:18,910
and I owe him a favor.

276
00:11:19,240 --> 00:11:20,700
Just help me out, will you?

277
00:11:21,720 --> 00:11:22,590
As a friend,

278
00:11:22,720 --> 00:11:23,840
let me give you a piece of advice:

279
00:11:23,840 --> 00:11:24,640
stay out of it.

280
00:11:24,960 --> 00:11:26,390
You'll only make enemies.

281
00:11:26,390 --> 00:11:26,910
Why?

282
00:11:30,170 --> 00:11:30,680
This case,

283
00:11:30,680 --> 00:11:31,910
back when it was still
at your procuratorate,

284
00:11:31,910 --> 00:11:33,120
was returned several times

285
00:11:33,120 --> 00:11:35,120
for supplementary investigation.

286
00:11:35,150 --> 00:11:36,080
Then, after it reached the court,

287
00:11:36,080 --> 00:11:37,120
it was sent back several times again.

288
00:11:37,120 --> 00:11:38,150
We went through hell

289
00:11:38,150 --> 00:11:39,390
and finally got this case to a verdict.

290
00:11:39,390 --> 00:11:40,510
Just think about the pressure

291
00:11:40,510 --> 00:11:41,310
we were under.

292
00:11:43,360 --> 00:11:44,000
Indeed.

293
00:11:48,000 --> 00:11:49,730
But doesn't that just prove...

294
00:11:50,460 --> 00:11:51,600
there's something wrong with the case?

295
00:11:51,600 --> 00:11:52,360
Cut it out.

296
00:11:52,960 --> 00:11:54,440
The fact that the court eventually

297
00:11:54,440 --> 00:11:55,360
convicted him shows

298
00:11:55,360 --> 00:11:56,480
that the basic facts were clear

299
00:11:56,480 --> 00:11:58,680
and the basic evidence was conclusive.

300
00:11:59,150 --> 00:12:00,670
This case has nothing to do with me,

301
00:12:00,670 --> 00:12:01,910
but if anyone starts picking it apart,

302
00:12:01,910 --> 00:12:03,030
I don't want to hear it.

303
00:12:03,030 --> 00:12:04,230
Then what if I told you

304
00:12:05,200 --> 00:12:06,910
it might actually have been
a wrongful conviction

305
00:12:06,910 --> 00:12:08,390
and that the real killer
could still be out there?

306
00:12:08,390 --> 00:12:10,390
Would you want to hear about it then?

307
00:12:12,470 --> 00:12:13,600
Just tell me

308
00:12:14,030 --> 00:12:15,120
who was in charge.

309
00:12:15,140 --> 00:12:16,800
I promise I won't sell you out.

310
00:12:20,790 --> 00:12:21,850
Let's have a match.

311
00:12:23,460 --> 00:12:24,320
Are you going to tell me

312
00:12:24,320 --> 00:12:25,180
if I win or lose?

313
00:12:25,630 --> 00:12:26,760
We'll see how I feel!

314
00:12:40,270 --> 00:12:40,930
Freeze!

315
00:12:40,930 --> 00:12:42,000
-Out of the way!
-Thief!

316
00:12:42,000 --> 00:12:42,720
My bag!

317
00:12:42,750 --> 00:12:43,150
Out of the way!

318
00:12:43,150 --> 00:12:43,910
Help!

319
00:12:43,910 --> 00:12:44,320
Move! Move!

320
00:12:44,320 --> 00:12:44,780
Freeze!

321
00:12:45,000 --> 00:12:45,440
Freeze!

322
00:12:45,440 --> 00:12:46,150
Thief!

323
00:12:46,870 --> 00:12:47,670
Make way!

324
00:12:47,910 --> 00:12:49,150
-Freeze!
-What are you doing?

325
00:12:49,150 --> 00:12:50,080
-Are you crazy?
-Freeze!

326
00:12:50,080 --> 00:12:50,670
Careful! Be careful!

327
00:12:50,670 --> 00:12:51,600
Stop! Don't run!

328
00:12:51,670 --> 00:12:52,330
Be careful!

329
00:12:52,480 --> 00:12:54,080
-Stop!
-Freeze! Be careful!

330
00:12:54,440 --> 00:12:54,910
Watch out!

331
00:12:54,910 --> 00:12:56,030
Come back! Come back!

332
00:12:56,030 --> 00:12:56,490
Freeze!

333
00:12:56,790 --> 00:12:57,270
Freeze!

334
00:12:58,080 --> 00:12:58,870
-Freeze!
-Don't run!

335
00:12:58,870 --> 00:12:59,440
My bag!

336
00:12:59,630 --> 00:13:00,090
Freeze!

337
00:13:00,840 --> 00:13:01,910
Give me back my bag!

338
00:13:02,510 --> 00:13:03,030
Freeze!

339
00:13:03,320 --> 00:13:03,910
My bag!

340
00:13:04,270 --> 00:13:05,330
Give me back my bag!

341
00:13:10,550 --> 00:13:11,010
Freeze!

342
00:13:11,440 --> 00:13:12,040
Don't run!

343
00:13:17,630 --> 00:13:18,120
Freeze!

344
00:13:24,720 --> 00:13:25,380
Don't move!

345
00:13:25,960 --> 00:13:26,620
Stay still!

346
00:13:30,390 --> 00:13:31,450
Quick, c-cuff him!

347
00:13:32,080 --> 00:13:32,540
Come on.

348
00:13:33,840 --> 00:13:34,500
Don't move!

349
00:13:35,600 --> 00:13:36,440
Captain Lyu?

350
00:13:37,120 --> 00:13:38,080
Why are you here?

351
00:13:39,670 --> 00:13:40,930
You're really clumsy.

352
00:13:43,510 --> 00:13:43,910
Hurry.

353
00:13:46,120 --> 00:13:46,750
Cuff him.

354
00:13:47,600 --> 00:13:49,030
You owe me money for my groceries!

355
00:13:49,030 --> 00:13:49,440
Okay!

356
00:13:56,440 --> 00:13:57,100
Who's that?

357
00:13:57,510 --> 00:13:58,480
Captain Lyu.

358
00:13:59,200 --> 00:13:59,960
He's the Captain Lyu you always

359
00:13:59,960 --> 00:14:00,620
talk about?

360
00:14:00,910 --> 00:14:02,030
Yes, a legend.

361
00:14:03,150 --> 00:14:04,610
Why did he retire so young?

362
00:14:04,910 --> 00:14:05,510
It seems

363
00:14:06,000 --> 00:14:08,000
he got disciplined over something.

364
00:14:09,120 --> 00:14:10,030
Come on, pull him up and take him away.

365
00:14:10,030 --> 00:14:10,470
Get up!

366
00:14:13,240 --> 00:14:13,640
Get up!

367
00:14:14,720 --> 00:14:15,850
Still trying to run?

368
00:14:23,270 --> 00:14:23,870
And then?

369
00:14:25,290 --> 00:14:26,960
Hey, quit rolling your eyes at me.

370
00:14:26,960 --> 00:14:28,240
Lyu, you're late!

371
00:14:28,270 --> 00:14:30,270
We've been waiting for you for ages!

372
00:14:31,790 --> 00:14:32,320
Let's go.

373
00:14:33,030 --> 00:14:35,360
Let's go play arcade games. Let's go.

374
00:14:36,730 --> 00:14:38,460
We can play arcade games again.

375
00:15:07,150 --> 00:15:07,810
Who are you?

376
00:15:10,080 --> 00:15:11,440
I'm with the Municipal Procuratorate.

377
00:15:11,440 --> 00:15:12,840
My name is Zheng Jianmin.

378
00:15:20,120 --> 00:15:21,050
Why are you here?

379
00:15:21,970 --> 00:15:23,570
It's about Yan Jicai's case.

380
00:15:23,600 --> 00:15:24,100
There are a few things

381
00:15:24,100 --> 00:15:25,500
I'd like to ask you about.

382
00:15:32,960 --> 00:15:33,790
I'm retired.

383
00:15:34,270 --> 00:15:36,070
Don't come looking for me again.

384
00:15:41,320 --> 00:15:42,150
Play for a while and hurry home

385
00:15:42,150 --> 00:15:43,280
to do your homework.

386
00:15:59,670 --> 00:16:01,000
I knew you'd hit a wall.

387
00:16:02,200 --> 00:16:03,150
He's notorious for being difficult.

388
00:16:03,150 --> 00:16:04,150
Hard to deal with.

389
00:16:04,270 --> 00:16:05,270
You knew that and didn't warn me?

390
00:16:05,270 --> 00:16:06,600
You did that on purpose?

391
00:16:07,790 --> 00:16:10,120
You think I'd take that punch for nothing?

392
00:16:14,670 --> 00:16:16,870
Before, you said he took early retirement.

393
00:16:16,870 --> 00:16:17,810
What happened?

394
00:16:18,150 --> 00:16:19,670
Nobody wants to deal with him.

395
00:16:19,670 --> 00:16:21,730
You'd better not ask around about it.

396
00:16:24,320 --> 00:16:26,250
Was it related to Yan Jicai's case?

397
00:16:29,360 --> 00:16:29,710
Well,

398
00:16:29,730 --> 00:16:30,670
why are you so obsessed

399
00:16:30,670 --> 00:16:31,530
with that case?

400
00:16:34,430 --> 00:16:35,270
I heard that the prosecutor

401
00:16:35,270 --> 00:16:36,400
from Bieshan has you

402
00:16:36,410 --> 00:16:37,940
wrapped around her finger.

403
00:16:38,960 --> 00:16:41,220
Are you working undercover for her, huh?

404
00:16:43,200 --> 00:16:43,790
Yes.

405
00:16:44,720 --> 00:16:45,750
I'm helping her.

406
00:16:46,080 --> 00:16:47,390
I won't hide it from you,
and I couldn't hide it anyway.

407
00:16:47,390 --> 00:16:49,720
You're a veteran criminal investigator.

408
00:16:50,150 --> 00:16:51,150
Your girlfriend?

409
00:16:51,870 --> 00:16:52,530
Not really.

410
00:16:55,630 --> 00:16:57,560
Keep this between us for now, okay?

411
00:16:57,600 --> 00:16:58,550
Otherwise, it'll be hard for me

412
00:16:58,550 --> 00:16:59,750
to make any progress.

413
00:17:07,349 --> 00:17:08,210
Zheng Jianmin.

414
00:17:09,550 --> 00:17:10,270
Listen to me—

415
00:17:10,270 --> 00:17:11,750
this is the second time I'm warning you.

416
00:17:11,750 --> 00:17:13,210
I won't say it a third time.

417
00:17:13,960 --> 00:17:14,690
If you really

418
00:17:15,160 --> 00:17:17,220
side with that prisoner on this case,

419
00:17:17,720 --> 00:17:19,790
you'll truly become everyone's enemy.

420
00:17:19,790 --> 00:17:21,349
Do you still want to stay in Nanlu?

421
00:17:21,349 --> 00:17:22,880
Because one thing is certain—

422
00:17:22,880 --> 00:17:25,560
you definitely won't be able to
stay at the Procuratorate anymore.

423
00:17:25,560 --> 00:17:26,349
Is it really that serious?

424
00:17:26,349 --> 00:17:27,000
It is.

425
00:17:28,180 --> 00:17:28,880
Do you know how many people

426
00:17:28,880 --> 00:17:30,010
this case involved?

427
00:17:30,330 --> 00:17:31,200
So it really could be

428
00:17:31,200 --> 00:17:32,510
a wrongful conviction.

429
00:17:32,510 --> 00:17:33,750
We can't just turn a blind eye
to a possible injustice

430
00:17:33,750 --> 00:17:36,410
just because many people
were involved, right?

431
00:17:41,790 --> 00:17:42,310
Tell me,

432
00:17:43,790 --> 00:17:44,520
from our side

433
00:17:45,310 --> 00:17:46,000
to yours

434
00:17:46,240 --> 00:17:47,500
and then to the courts—

435
00:17:47,680 --> 00:17:49,880
who would deliberately set out

436
00:17:49,880 --> 00:17:50,880
to create a wrongful conviction?

437
00:17:50,880 --> 00:17:51,680
No one, right?

438
00:17:53,240 --> 00:17:54,680
We didn't know the suspect.

439
00:17:54,680 --> 00:17:55,640
We had no personal grudge against him.

440
00:17:55,640 --> 00:17:57,900
So why would we deliberately target him?

441
00:17:58,240 --> 00:17:59,270
The police, the procuratorate,
and the court

442
00:17:59,270 --> 00:18:00,940
investigated it back and forth
so many times,

443
00:18:00,940 --> 00:18:02,920
and in the end still convicted him.
What does that mean?

444
00:18:02,920 --> 00:18:04,050
What does that mean?

445
00:18:04,200 --> 00:18:05,030
Four words:

446
00:18:05,790 --> 00:18:07,050
"Cannot be ruled out."

447
00:18:08,440 --> 00:18:10,270
How can you say that

448
00:18:10,270 --> 00:18:11,960
like it's perfectly justified?

449
00:18:11,960 --> 00:18:13,000
What if?

450
00:18:13,510 --> 00:18:15,310
I mean, even if there's only
a one-in-a-million chance

451
00:18:15,310 --> 00:18:16,550
that he wasn't the real killer—

452
00:18:16,550 --> 00:18:17,150
then what?

453
00:18:17,270 --> 00:18:18,240
We just leave it be

454
00:18:18,240 --> 00:18:19,510
and let the innocent man
remain wrongfully convicted?

455
00:18:19,510 --> 00:18:20,270
No, shouldn't those 4 words instead be

456
00:18:20,270 --> 00:18:22,130
"innocent until proven guilty"?

457
00:18:23,440 --> 00:18:24,110
You punk,

458
00:18:24,110 --> 00:18:24,940
how did you learn to be

459
00:18:24,940 --> 00:18:26,000
so sanctimonious?

460
00:18:27,830 --> 00:18:28,880
That female prosecutor from Bieshan

461
00:18:28,880 --> 00:18:30,280
fed you that, didn't she?

462
00:18:34,010 --> 00:18:34,680
I heard she's

463
00:18:34,680 --> 00:18:36,310
a PhD from a top university.

464
00:18:37,790 --> 00:18:38,520
Good for you.

465
00:18:39,440 --> 00:18:40,550
You lucky bastard...

466
00:18:40,550 --> 00:18:42,270
We're talking about the wrongful conviction.
Stop changing the subject!

467
00:18:42,270 --> 00:18:43,870
Why do you have so much to say?

468
00:18:45,310 --> 00:18:46,170
Fine, I'm full.

469
00:18:48,510 --> 00:18:50,240
I have something to do. I'm out.

470
00:18:50,480 --> 00:18:51,210
Pay the bill.

471
00:18:51,750 --> 00:18:52,200
Wait.

472
00:18:54,140 --> 00:18:55,640
So did Captain Lyu's early retirement

473
00:18:55,640 --> 00:18:56,550
have anything to do with

474
00:18:56,550 --> 00:18:57,550
Yan Jicai's case?

475
00:18:57,550 --> 00:18:59,160
Yes and no.

476
00:18:59,550 --> 00:19:00,640
What do you mean?

477
00:19:08,920 --> 00:19:10,790
Suspected of
extracting a confession through torture.

478
00:19:10,790 --> 00:19:12,400
Actually, he just got so angry

479
00:19:12,400 --> 00:19:13,430
during the interrogation

480
00:19:13,430 --> 00:19:15,830
that he gave the bastard who molested
the little girl a couple of slaps.

481
00:19:15,830 --> 00:19:16,750
He hit a bit too hard

482
00:19:16,750 --> 00:19:18,210
and gave him a concussion.

483
00:19:19,830 --> 00:19:20,680
What does that have to do

484
00:19:20,680 --> 00:19:21,940
with Yan Jicai's case?

485
00:19:22,750 --> 00:19:24,960
Well, do you really think,
with Lyu's temper,

486
00:19:24,960 --> 00:19:25,790
he could've kept himself under control

487
00:19:25,790 --> 00:19:27,390
when dealing with Yan Jicai?

488
00:19:28,240 --> 00:19:29,300
If that kind of scum

489
00:19:29,590 --> 00:19:30,790
fell into my hands...

490
00:19:33,830 --> 00:19:35,490
I'd be the one to lose my badge.

491
00:19:38,270 --> 00:19:39,400
Uncle Hu, Uncle Hu!

492
00:19:39,830 --> 00:19:41,550
Yin Ping's grandma hanged herself!

493
00:19:41,550 --> 00:19:42,030
What?

494
00:19:44,070 --> 00:19:45,160
Xia, don't go!

495
00:19:46,110 --> 00:19:46,880
You can't go.

496
00:19:47,310 --> 00:19:47,770
I'll go!

497
00:19:58,030 --> 00:19:58,710
Officers,

498
00:19:58,790 --> 00:20:00,050
did Hu Xudong confess?

499
00:20:00,270 --> 00:20:01,680
The whole family died.

500
00:20:01,830 --> 00:20:03,160
This is just too tragic.

501
00:20:03,350 --> 00:20:04,870
You can't let the killer
get away with this!

502
00:20:04,870 --> 00:20:06,270
Yeah! Don't let the killer get away!

503
00:20:06,270 --> 00:20:07,400
Don't let the killer get away!

504
00:20:07,400 --> 00:20:08,590
Don't let him get away!

505
00:20:08,590 --> 00:20:09,880
Don't let the killer get away!

506
00:20:09,880 --> 00:20:11,510
Calm down, everyone! Calm down!

507
00:20:11,510 --> 00:20:13,200
The case is still under investigation.

508
00:20:13,200 --> 00:20:14,030
Just wait a little longer.

509
00:20:14,030 --> 00:20:15,160
How can we calm down?

510
00:20:15,480 --> 00:20:16,740
What are you all doing—

511
00:20:17,030 --> 00:20:17,680
playing around?

512
00:20:17,680 --> 00:20:18,510
Judge Hu,

513
00:20:18,830 --> 00:20:19,940
the killer must be shot!

514
00:20:19,940 --> 00:20:20,590
What do you mean, "shot"?

515
00:20:20,590 --> 00:20:21,030
Shoot him!

516
00:20:21,030 --> 00:20:21,960
Don't talk nonsense!

517
00:20:21,960 --> 00:20:23,790
-Shoot him!
-Shoot him!

518
00:20:23,880 --> 00:20:25,750
Investigating a case takes time!

519
00:20:26,030 --> 00:20:27,680
You must have faith in the law!

520
00:20:27,680 --> 00:20:29,070
Fellow villagers, listen to me.

521
00:20:29,070 --> 00:20:29,960
Hu is right.

522
00:20:30,550 --> 00:20:31,960
You have to trust the government

523
00:20:31,960 --> 00:20:32,960
and trust the law!

524
00:20:33,200 --> 00:20:34,750
Hu Xudong's second uncle
is on the township committee!

525
00:20:34,750 --> 00:20:36,950
He'll definitely cover for his nephew!

526
00:20:38,920 --> 00:20:39,990
That won't do!

527
00:20:40,110 --> 00:20:41,680
The whole family died for nothing!

528
00:20:41,680 --> 00:20:42,350
Stop talking.

529
00:20:42,350 --> 00:20:44,030
We want justice

530
00:20:44,240 --> 00:20:45,570
for Yin Ping's grandma!

531
00:20:46,030 --> 00:20:47,290
Don't move! Stop them!

532
00:21:13,440 --> 00:21:14,400
Come out quickly!

533
00:21:14,400 --> 00:21:15,000
No, no, no!

534
00:21:16,000 --> 00:21:16,930
Get him out here!

535
00:21:18,030 --> 00:21:19,360
-Come out!
-Don't move!

536
00:21:20,960 --> 00:21:21,890
I'm telling you,

537
00:21:21,960 --> 00:21:23,880
until we know exactly what happened,

538
00:21:23,880 --> 00:21:25,210
don't do anything rash!

539
00:21:35,920 --> 00:21:37,000
Don't get so worked up!

540
00:21:37,000 --> 00:21:37,530
Get down!

541
00:21:38,160 --> 00:21:39,490
Don't do anything rash!

542
00:22:15,790 --> 00:22:16,520
Understood.

543
00:22:18,350 --> 00:22:19,080
Understood.

544
00:22:19,880 --> 00:22:20,600
Hu, do this:

545
00:22:21,550 --> 00:22:22,640
tell Xia Yingjie to come back immediately.

546
00:22:22,640 --> 00:22:24,000
Don't delay even a minute.

547
00:22:24,000 --> 00:22:26,000
Just say it's the court's decision.

548
00:22:27,550 --> 00:22:27,920
Okay.

549
00:22:40,030 --> 00:22:41,090
Is this case really

550
00:22:41,100 --> 00:22:42,350
causing that much of an uproar right now?

551
00:22:42,350 --> 00:22:42,750
Yes.

552
00:22:43,590 --> 00:22:45,010
So I'm thinking of

553
00:22:45,680 --> 00:22:47,810
transferring Xia Yingjie back first.

554
00:22:50,450 --> 00:22:51,720
Even though her disciplinary period
isn't over yet,

555
00:22:51,720 --> 00:22:52,550
we can hold off

556
00:22:52,570 --> 00:22:54,070
on restoring her to her regular post

557
00:22:54,070 --> 00:22:55,240
and let her do some other work

558
00:22:55,240 --> 00:22:57,640
in the archives or administration for now.

559
00:22:58,920 --> 00:23:00,350
Xia's personality,

560
00:23:01,030 --> 00:23:01,640
really...

561
00:23:02,830 --> 00:23:04,030
She has a good nature,

562
00:23:04,550 --> 00:23:06,350
and she's highly competent professionally.

563
00:23:06,350 --> 00:23:08,080
But she's just too idealistic.

564
00:23:08,880 --> 00:23:10,270
She doesn't think things through

565
00:23:10,270 --> 00:23:11,930
and tends to act impulsively.

566
00:23:13,680 --> 00:23:15,340
Now that the old lady has died,

567
00:23:15,680 --> 00:23:16,350
I'm afraid public opinion

568
00:23:16,350 --> 00:23:17,950
may drag our court into this.

569
00:23:18,480 --> 00:23:20,350
So I'm thinking of
transferring her back first,

570
00:23:20,350 --> 00:23:22,000
away from the center of the incident.

571
00:23:22,000 --> 00:23:23,790
It'd be better for both her and us.

572
00:23:23,790 --> 00:23:24,480
What if the villagers

573
00:23:24,480 --> 00:23:25,610
cause some trouble?

574
00:23:26,110 --> 00:23:26,640
At least once she's back here,

575
00:23:26,640 --> 00:23:28,840
her personal safety will be protected.

576
00:23:29,110 --> 00:23:30,370
A female comrade out
at the grassroots level

577
00:23:30,370 --> 00:23:31,230
is somewhat...

578
00:23:36,880 --> 00:23:38,080
Let me think about it.

579
00:23:52,310 --> 00:23:53,170
Alright, then.

580
00:23:53,590 --> 00:23:54,270
I agree.

581
00:23:55,720 --> 00:23:57,030
As for how to arrange her position

582
00:23:57,030 --> 00:23:58,000
after bringing her back,

583
00:23:58,000 --> 00:23:59,350
how to minimize the impact,

584
00:23:59,350 --> 00:24:00,830
and how to prevent gossip

585
00:24:00,830 --> 00:24:01,420
among colleagues—

586
00:24:01,420 --> 00:24:02,350
you handle that.

587
00:24:02,480 --> 00:24:03,210
Understood.

588
00:24:03,590 --> 00:24:04,640
After all, Judge Mei

589
00:24:04,640 --> 00:24:05,510
has already been removed from her post,

590
00:24:05,510 --> 00:24:06,310
while Xia

591
00:24:06,480 --> 00:24:07,590
was sent there for a couple of days

592
00:24:07,590 --> 00:24:08,480
and is now being transferred back again.

593
00:24:08,480 --> 00:24:09,940
It doesn't look very fair.

594
00:24:10,310 --> 00:24:10,910
Of course,

595
00:24:11,000 --> 00:24:12,000
personally, I hope

596
00:24:12,000 --> 00:24:12,860
she comes back.

597
00:24:13,270 --> 00:24:13,920
Keeping her down at the grassroots level

598
00:24:13,920 --> 00:24:15,050
is a waste of her talent.

599
00:24:15,050 --> 00:24:16,640
Her abilities are being squandered.

600
00:24:16,640 --> 00:24:17,790
Don't worry, Court Pres. Qiu.

601
00:24:17,790 --> 00:24:19,190
I'll definitely be fair.

602
00:24:19,830 --> 00:24:22,000
Here, have another rib.

603
00:24:22,380 --> 00:24:23,110
Thank you.

604
00:24:24,270 --> 00:24:25,550
Eat well, worry less,

605
00:24:25,750 --> 00:24:28,080
and you'll stay healthy for years to come.

606
00:24:28,590 --> 00:24:30,250
Why did you cook so much today?

607
00:24:30,400 --> 00:24:31,070
Eat more.

608
00:24:33,550 --> 00:24:34,810
Don't go back tonight.

609
00:24:34,880 --> 00:24:35,510
Stay here.

610
00:24:36,000 --> 00:24:37,790
In a couple of days, I'll arrange a car

611
00:24:37,790 --> 00:24:39,450
and take you back to Binjiang.

612
00:24:39,830 --> 00:24:40,510
Why?

613
00:24:42,350 --> 00:24:43,810
I've already discussed it

614
00:24:44,310 --> 00:24:45,810
with your Deputy Court Pres. Yu.

615
00:24:45,810 --> 00:24:46,740
For your safety,

616
00:24:46,880 --> 00:24:47,810
and to avoid some

617
00:24:47,880 --> 00:24:49,810
unnecessary public controversy,

618
00:24:49,960 --> 00:24:51,310
you should go back first.

619
00:24:51,310 --> 00:24:53,110
As for what you'll do when you get back,

620
00:24:53,110 --> 00:24:55,310
just follow the court's arrangements.

621
00:24:55,480 --> 00:24:56,480
You tattled on me.

622
00:24:57,680 --> 00:24:58,160
Yes.

623
00:24:59,170 --> 00:25:00,260
I tattled on you.

624
00:25:01,880 --> 00:25:02,550
For the past few days,

625
00:25:02,550 --> 00:25:04,160
I've been on edge all night, every night—

626
00:25:04,160 --> 00:25:05,310
I haven't been able to
sleep and have had to

627
00:25:05,310 --> 00:25:06,400
get up to use the bathroom
several times a night.

628
00:25:06,400 --> 00:25:08,130
Ask her if you don't believe me.

629
00:25:08,240 --> 00:25:09,680
He was worried about you.

630
00:25:09,880 --> 00:25:11,720
When he went to the bathroom outside,

631
00:25:11,720 --> 00:25:13,780
he'd stop by your room to check on you.

632
00:25:17,000 --> 00:25:17,720
Mentor,

633
00:25:18,790 --> 00:25:19,400
thank you.

634
00:25:20,350 --> 00:25:21,480
What did you call me?

635
00:25:21,880 --> 00:25:22,750
Mentor.

636
00:25:25,000 --> 00:25:26,330
She called me "Mentor."

637
00:25:27,720 --> 00:25:29,780
You graduated from a top university,

638
00:25:30,010 --> 00:25:31,520
and you're a judge at

639
00:25:31,550 --> 00:25:32,920
the Municipal Intermediate People's Court.

640
00:25:32,920 --> 00:25:34,750
How could I possibly be your mentor?

641
00:25:34,750 --> 00:25:36,030
I don't care whether you like it or not—

642
00:25:36,030 --> 00:25:37,630
I'm calling you that anyway.

643
00:25:37,640 --> 00:25:38,700
I'm not going back.

644
00:25:40,590 --> 00:25:41,580
Look at this kid.

645
00:25:42,030 --> 00:25:43,360
You have to listen to me.

646
00:25:45,480 --> 00:25:46,030
No, Mentor,

647
00:25:46,030 --> 00:25:47,050
do you really think Hu Xudong

648
00:25:47,050 --> 00:25:47,730
killed him?

649
00:25:48,160 --> 00:25:49,310
What was his motive?

650
00:25:49,310 --> 00:25:49,680
I...

651
00:25:50,310 --> 00:25:52,170
I just can't get my head around it.

652
00:25:53,510 --> 00:25:54,910
Right now in the village,

653
00:25:55,270 --> 00:25:56,830
nine out of ten people think

654
00:25:57,880 --> 00:25:59,210
Hu Xudong is the killer.

655
00:26:00,110 --> 00:26:01,880
What... do you think?

656
00:26:02,550 --> 00:26:04,030
They jumped to conclusions,

657
00:26:04,030 --> 00:26:06,030
letting their own biases sway them.

658
00:26:06,160 --> 00:26:08,310
If you really want to
keep pursuing this case,

659
00:26:08,310 --> 00:26:10,680
then you have even more reason
to go back to Binjiang.

660
00:26:10,680 --> 00:26:11,550
Because this case

661
00:26:11,550 --> 00:26:13,550
will end up before the court anyway.

662
00:26:13,750 --> 00:26:14,750
You'll be more useful

663
00:26:14,750 --> 00:26:16,110
in Binjiang than here.

664
00:26:21,210 --> 00:26:22,310
That thing I've asked you
to help with earlier—

665
00:26:22,310 --> 00:26:23,460
about my dad's comrade-in-arms—

666
00:26:23,460 --> 00:26:24,110
did you ask about it?

667
00:26:24,110 --> 00:26:25,070
"Go into villages

668
00:26:25,070 --> 00:26:27,310
and carry out legal education programs.

669
00:26:27,310 --> 00:26:29,510
The legal outreach teams
take root in the fields,

670
00:26:29,510 --> 00:26:31,030
using evening legal classes,

671
00:26:31,030 --> 00:26:32,230
film screenings..."

672
00:26:34,350 --> 00:26:35,410
I'm talking to you.

673
00:26:36,200 --> 00:26:37,440
His case is under the civil division.

674
00:26:37,440 --> 00:26:39,770
It's not appropriate for me to interfere.

675
00:26:40,830 --> 00:26:42,200
Then just ask around

676
00:26:42,270 --> 00:26:43,750
and show some concern. Is that so hard?

677
00:26:43,750 --> 00:26:44,940
Wouldn't asking about it itself
be taking a position?

678
00:26:44,940 --> 00:26:45,730
I'm the deputy president of the court.

679
00:26:45,730 --> 00:26:47,240
What would my colleagues think of me?

680
00:26:47,240 --> 00:26:49,110
Then let them think whatever they want.

681
00:26:49,110 --> 00:26:49,640
Isn't that exactly

682
00:26:49,640 --> 00:26:50,590
the point?

683
00:26:51,200 --> 00:26:51,510
Then,

684
00:26:51,510 --> 00:26:54,110
what do we need you,
the deputy president, for?

685
00:26:55,000 --> 00:26:57,240
Did your dad make me
the deputy court president?

686
00:26:57,240 --> 00:26:58,240
Am I in this position

687
00:26:58,240 --> 00:26:59,000
just to serve your family and pull strings

688
00:26:59,000 --> 00:27:00,250
for your dad's old comrade-in-arms?

689
00:27:00,250 --> 00:27:01,240
Watch how you talk.

690
00:27:01,240 --> 00:27:02,040
How should I talk then?

691
00:27:02,040 --> 00:27:02,830
So after all these years,

692
00:27:02,830 --> 00:27:04,160
my family hasn't helped you at all?

693
00:27:04,160 --> 00:27:06,890
Don't you think
you're being vulgar saying this?

694
00:27:07,400 --> 00:27:08,110
I'm vulgar.

695
00:27:09,070 --> 00:27:10,530
Xia Yingjie isn't vulgar.

696
00:27:11,030 --> 00:27:12,280
You're so tender and protective of her,

697
00:27:12,280 --> 00:27:13,270
caring for her in every way.

698
00:27:13,270 --> 00:27:15,000
No, what are you talking about?

699
00:27:15,110 --> 00:27:16,070
The TV program's director

700
00:27:16,070 --> 00:27:17,070
was my classmate.

701
00:27:17,310 --> 00:27:18,240
They weren't allowed to report it,

702
00:27:18,240 --> 00:27:19,330
but she told me

703
00:27:19,480 --> 00:27:20,110
that if Xia Yingjie had not

704
00:27:20,110 --> 00:27:21,200
let that mentally ill man out,

705
00:27:21,200 --> 00:27:22,460
he wouldn't have died.

706
00:27:22,590 --> 00:27:23,790
You just like that type—

707
00:27:23,790 --> 00:27:24,680
someone with personality.

708
00:27:24,680 --> 00:27:25,240
Oh, right.

709
00:27:25,240 --> 00:27:26,590
She wants
absolutely nothing to do with you.

710
00:27:26,590 --> 00:27:27,720
Are you done?

711
00:27:41,550 --> 00:27:42,880
Other people's business

712
00:27:42,880 --> 00:27:44,080
is always important.

713
00:27:45,000 --> 00:27:45,590
But when it comes to our family,

714
00:27:45,590 --> 00:27:47,250
I'm just being unreasonable.

715
00:27:49,880 --> 00:27:51,960
We're legally married, after all.

716
00:27:52,790 --> 00:27:54,110
Are you really not going to help?

717
00:27:54,110 --> 00:27:54,880
Fine, I won't argue with you.

718
00:27:54,880 --> 00:27:56,080
I'll go ask tomorrow.

719
00:27:56,160 --> 00:27:56,490
Okay?

720
00:27:57,070 --> 00:27:58,310
But let me make this clear:

721
00:27:58,310 --> 00:27:59,170
I'm just asking,

722
00:27:59,170 --> 00:27:59,920
not interfering,

723
00:27:59,920 --> 00:28:01,020
and I won't take any position.

724
00:28:01,020 --> 00:28:02,080
Do you understand?

725
00:28:04,880 --> 00:28:05,740
Satisfied now?

726
00:28:06,110 --> 00:28:06,770
Satisfied.

727
00:28:06,920 --> 00:28:07,270
Good.

728
00:28:20,350 --> 00:28:22,510
Stay here and play, kid. Don't run around.

729
00:28:22,510 --> 00:28:23,030
Okay.

730
00:29:14,070 --> 00:29:14,830
Big Bottle,

731
00:29:15,550 --> 00:29:17,550
did you forget to bring your bottle?

732
00:29:18,750 --> 00:29:20,240
Here, I'll lend this to you.

733
00:29:20,240 --> 00:29:21,040
It works well.

734
00:29:21,960 --> 00:29:22,820
Let me tell you.

735
00:29:23,510 --> 00:29:24,440
In my eyes,

736
00:29:24,440 --> 00:29:25,970
you'll always be a bastard!

737
00:29:26,510 --> 00:29:28,770
What are you looking at? Get back to work!

738
00:29:34,270 --> 00:29:34,870
Yan Jicai!

739
00:29:35,150 --> 00:29:36,350
-Stop! Stop!
-Child!

740
00:29:36,680 --> 00:29:37,640
-That child!
-Stop!

741
00:29:37,640 --> 00:29:38,000
Stop!

742
00:29:38,000 --> 00:29:39,070
Yan Jicai, stop!

743
00:29:39,110 --> 00:29:40,440
Stop! Stop right there!

744
00:29:40,510 --> 00:29:41,370
-Child!
-Stop!

745
00:29:51,110 --> 00:29:51,880
Get a rope quickly.

746
00:29:51,880 --> 00:29:52,480
Save them.

747
00:29:53,030 --> 00:29:53,630
Yan Jicai!

748
00:29:53,920 --> 00:29:54,680
Be careful!

749
00:29:55,070 --> 00:29:55,480
Girl,

750
00:29:56,720 --> 00:29:57,480
don't move.

751
00:30:04,010 --> 00:30:04,590
Thank you.

752
00:30:04,590 --> 00:30:05,440
Thank you for saving our child.

753
00:30:05,440 --> 00:30:06,000
Get up quickly.

754
00:30:06,000 --> 00:30:06,930
With this merit,

755
00:30:07,310 --> 00:30:09,770
he'll get
at least 6 months off his sentence.

756
00:30:10,680 --> 00:30:11,830
That Big Bottle...

757
00:30:20,440 --> 00:30:21,970
Mentor, you're taking medicine again?

758
00:30:21,970 --> 00:30:24,070
I'm basically a walking pharmacy now.

759
00:30:24,070 --> 00:30:25,530
I can't manage without it.

760
00:30:26,200 --> 00:30:26,920
You should find some time

761
00:30:26,920 --> 00:30:28,380
to get a thorough checkup.

762
00:30:29,440 --> 00:30:30,000
Mr. Guo.

763
00:30:31,110 --> 00:30:32,040
These are yours.

764
00:30:32,920 --> 00:30:33,590
Let me see.

765
00:30:33,920 --> 00:30:35,120
There's none for you.

766
00:30:37,000 --> 00:30:38,510
Whose letter are you waiting for?

767
00:30:38,510 --> 00:30:39,450
Your boyfriend's?

768
00:30:39,450 --> 00:30:41,110
Don't talk nonsense. I'm not.

769
00:30:41,830 --> 00:30:42,510
Who wasn't like this

770
00:30:42,510 --> 00:30:43,550
when we were young?

771
00:30:43,550 --> 00:30:44,390
I'm off, Mr. Guo.

772
00:30:44,390 --> 00:30:45,160
Go on, go on.

773
00:30:49,030 --> 00:30:51,030
Why hasn't a single reply come back?

774
00:30:51,030 --> 00:30:51,860
We formally

775
00:30:52,070 --> 00:30:53,640
submitted the request, after all.

776
00:30:53,640 --> 00:30:55,900
They should at least give a reply, right?

777
00:30:56,000 --> 00:30:56,930
What's the rush?

778
00:30:57,200 --> 00:30:59,270
If they don't reply,
just keep writing to them.

779
00:30:59,270 --> 00:31:01,600
Sooner or later, they'll have to respond.

780
00:31:03,640 --> 00:31:04,970
Then I'll keep writing.

781
00:31:06,400 --> 00:31:06,860
Mr. Guo.

782
00:31:07,400 --> 00:31:08,530
Sun wants to see you.

783
00:31:08,720 --> 00:31:10,720
Yan Jicai is causing trouble again.

784
00:31:12,160 --> 00:31:12,760
Him again.

785
00:31:12,850 --> 00:31:13,880
I don't want to live anymore!

786
00:31:13,880 --> 00:31:14,350
Behave!

787
00:31:14,400 --> 00:31:14,960
Shoot me!

788
00:31:15,030 --> 00:31:16,030
Behave yourself!

789
00:31:16,030 --> 00:31:17,550
Step back! Behave yourself!

790
00:31:17,550 --> 00:31:18,210
Yan Jicai!

791
00:31:18,310 --> 00:31:18,840
Shoot me!

792
00:31:19,160 --> 00:31:20,080
That's enough!

793
00:31:20,110 --> 00:31:21,110
Stop struggling!

794
00:31:21,110 --> 00:31:21,960
Enough already!

795
00:31:21,960 --> 00:31:22,960
Behave yourself!

796
00:31:23,270 --> 00:31:24,510
I don't want to live anymore!

797
00:31:24,510 --> 00:31:25,270
What happened here?

798
00:31:25,270 --> 00:31:25,830
Stay still!

799
00:31:25,830 --> 00:31:26,720
The No. 1 prisoner

800
00:31:26,720 --> 00:31:28,320
kept calling him Big Bottle,

801
00:31:28,550 --> 00:31:30,310
and he completely lost it today.

802
00:31:30,310 --> 00:31:31,370
Yan Jicai, behave!

803
00:31:31,400 --> 00:31:32,860
Yan Jicai, that's enough!

804
00:31:33,030 --> 00:31:33,720
Yan Jicai!

805
00:31:37,880 --> 00:31:39,000
Get lost, liars!

806
00:31:39,030 --> 00:31:39,790
Behave yourself!

807
00:31:39,790 --> 00:31:41,110
I'll never believe you people again!

808
00:31:41,110 --> 00:31:42,840
-I don't want to...
-Yan Jicai!

809
00:31:43,400 --> 00:31:44,930
What did we tell you before?

810
00:31:45,400 --> 00:31:47,550
Believe in the law. Believe in us.

811
00:31:48,640 --> 00:31:50,830
You can't even
handle this little grievance?

812
00:31:50,830 --> 00:31:51,770
You're liars!

813
00:31:51,920 --> 00:31:53,010
I don't believe you!

814
00:31:53,010 --> 00:31:53,830
Who lied to you?

815
00:31:53,830 --> 00:31:55,360
I'm telling you, we went...

816
00:31:56,510 --> 00:31:57,240
Release him.

817
00:31:58,200 --> 00:31:59,660
No, Mr. Guo. He's gone mad.

818
00:31:59,720 --> 00:32:01,650
He's not mad. I know what I'm doing.

819
00:32:01,720 --> 00:32:02,450
Release him.

820
00:32:06,870 --> 00:32:07,400
Come out.

821
00:32:11,070 --> 00:32:11,680
Yan Jicai.

822
00:32:13,790 --> 00:32:14,720
What do you want?

823
00:32:15,590 --> 00:32:16,520
Vent your anger.

824
00:32:17,200 --> 00:32:18,480
Bang your head against the wall.

825
00:32:18,480 --> 00:32:20,140
Do you still want to beat me up?

826
00:32:20,840 --> 00:32:21,920
Come on, I'll let you do it.

827
00:32:21,920 --> 00:32:23,320
Don't any of you stop him!

828
00:32:24,570 --> 00:32:25,880
Do you know how many times you've ended up

829
00:32:25,880 --> 00:32:26,940
on the prison's list of inmates

830
00:32:26,940 --> 00:32:28,110
who refuse to follow the rules?

831
00:32:28,110 --> 00:32:29,160
Even so,

832
00:32:29,240 --> 00:32:30,270
Prosecutor Zhang and I

833
00:32:30,270 --> 00:32:32,200
still chose to believe you!

834
00:32:34,110 --> 00:32:37,030
And we've genuinely made an effort!

835
00:32:38,320 --> 00:32:39,590
If you still don't believe us,

836
00:32:39,590 --> 00:32:41,350
then no one can help you.

837
00:32:41,590 --> 00:32:43,390
A person who believes in nothing

838
00:32:43,920 --> 00:32:44,590
has no hope

839
00:32:44,590 --> 00:32:45,680
for the future either.

840
00:32:45,680 --> 00:32:46,440
He won't last

841
00:32:46,440 --> 00:32:47,510
much longer in here...

842
00:32:47,510 --> 00:32:49,240
So I don't want to live anymore!

843
00:32:49,270 --> 00:32:50,400
You don't want to live anymore?

844
00:32:50,400 --> 00:32:51,680
You're going to abandon such a good wife?

845
00:32:51,680 --> 00:32:52,740
And your child too?

846
00:32:53,640 --> 00:32:54,700
"Such a good wife?"

847
00:32:55,510 --> 00:32:56,040
How good?

848
00:33:00,070 --> 00:33:01,330
You went to see my wife?

849
00:33:01,480 --> 00:33:02,080
Yan Jicai,

850
00:33:02,400 --> 00:33:03,830
take a good look at me, Guo Dajie,

851
00:33:03,830 --> 00:33:05,430
and Prosecutor Zhang Lihui.

852
00:33:05,440 --> 00:33:06,970
Take a good look at our faces!

853
00:33:06,970 --> 00:33:08,170
Do we look like liars?

854
00:33:10,400 --> 00:33:11,240
Even today,

855
00:33:11,400 --> 00:33:12,590
we still can't make

856
00:33:12,590 --> 00:33:13,720
any promises to you!

857
00:33:14,720 --> 00:33:16,920
We can only ask you to believe in the law!

858
00:33:18,920 --> 00:33:21,120
That's all I can say. Do you understand?

859
00:33:21,480 --> 00:33:23,540
So what if they call you "Big Bottle"?

860
00:33:24,400 --> 00:33:25,550
People used to call me

861
00:33:25,550 --> 00:33:26,550
"Ms. Guo!"

862
00:33:27,270 --> 00:33:27,940
Let them call you that.

863
00:33:27,940 --> 00:33:29,070
Why should you care?

864
00:33:31,720 --> 00:33:32,920
Reflect on yourself!

865
00:33:43,260 --> 00:33:47,090
[Binjiang Intermediate People's Court]

866
00:33:53,830 --> 00:33:55,090
Deputy Court Pres. Yu.

867
00:33:55,830 --> 00:33:57,830
Welcome back, Comrade Xia Yingjie.

868
00:33:59,160 --> 00:33:59,760
Thank you.

869
00:34:02,550 --> 00:34:03,750
You look pretty well.

870
00:34:06,310 --> 00:34:07,840
Put your things down first.

871
00:34:13,550 --> 00:34:14,370
Are you...

872
00:34:14,880 --> 00:34:15,810
living here now?

873
00:34:16,750 --> 00:34:17,750
Family conflict.

874
00:34:17,760 --> 00:34:19,190
I'm taking refuge here for a while.

875
00:34:19,190 --> 00:34:20,389
Go ahead, laugh at me.

876
00:34:22,150 --> 00:34:24,230
What right do I have to laugh at anyone?

877
00:34:24,230 --> 00:34:24,840
I've looked into

878
00:34:24,840 --> 00:34:26,030
what happened on your end.

879
00:34:26,030 --> 00:34:27,690
You didn't do anything wrong.

880
00:34:28,159 --> 00:34:29,480
The case is almost ready
to go to the procuratorate.

881
00:34:29,480 --> 00:34:31,940
I hear they've already approved
the arrest.

882
00:34:34,440 --> 00:34:35,040
Thank you.

883
00:34:35,110 --> 00:34:35,900
Rest for a bit.

884
00:34:35,900 --> 00:34:37,699
I'll go get you something to eat.

885
00:34:51,110 --> 00:34:51,920
Hello.

886
00:34:52,320 --> 00:34:52,719
Hello.

887
00:34:53,000 --> 00:34:54,760
Could you please get Chen Yizhong for me?

888
00:34:54,760 --> 00:34:55,820
Sure, please hold.

889
00:34:56,400 --> 00:34:57,730
Yizhong, phone for you.

890
00:34:59,320 --> 00:35:00,920
Hello, this is Chen Yizhong.

891
00:35:03,550 --> 00:35:03,950
Hello?

892
00:35:06,630 --> 00:35:07,030
Hello?

893
00:35:13,700 --> 00:35:15,730
They hung up.
Are you sure that was for me?

894
00:35:15,730 --> 00:35:16,770
Yes, it was.

895
00:35:17,840 --> 00:35:18,920
It was a woman

896
00:35:19,590 --> 00:35:20,630
with a nice voice.

897
00:35:44,020 --> 00:35:45,070
I really can't believe

898
00:35:45,070 --> 00:35:46,930
we haven't gotten a single reply.

899
00:35:47,050 --> 00:35:49,180
I mean, if it were a prisoner appealing

900
00:35:49,200 --> 00:35:50,110
and they ignored it
because they saw it too often,

901
00:35:50,110 --> 00:35:51,110
that would be one thing.

902
00:35:51,110 --> 00:35:52,440
But we're prosecutors—

903
00:35:52,590 --> 00:35:54,840
even when prosecutors help
a prisoner appeal,

904
00:35:54,840 --> 00:35:55,890
they still ignore it.

905
00:35:55,890 --> 00:35:56,920
Then how hard must it be for prisoners

906
00:35:56,920 --> 00:35:58,030
to appeal on their own?

907
00:35:58,030 --> 00:35:59,110
Didn't I tell you?

908
00:36:00,190 --> 00:36:01,760
We can't rush this.

909
00:36:04,800 --> 00:36:06,230
But I feel that Yan Jicai

910
00:36:06,400 --> 00:36:07,630
is about to break down.

911
00:36:07,630 --> 00:36:09,900
Something is bound to happen
sooner or later.

912
00:36:09,900 --> 00:36:11,560
Then we'll just keep writing.

913
00:36:11,900 --> 00:36:13,800
Keep reporting the case
to judicial authorities

914
00:36:13,800 --> 00:36:14,660
at every level.

915
00:36:15,110 --> 00:36:16,480
What other way is there?

916
00:36:19,920 --> 00:36:21,780
At this rate, it'll take forever.

917
00:36:23,230 --> 00:36:23,800
What?

918
00:36:25,000 --> 00:36:26,130
Can't wait anymore?

919
00:36:30,640 --> 00:36:32,110
Got someone else on your mind,

920
00:36:32,110 --> 00:36:32,750
huh?

921
00:36:33,970 --> 00:36:34,870
Mentor,

922
00:36:34,890 --> 00:36:36,760
I'm talking about serious business here!

923
00:36:36,760 --> 00:36:38,320
It's a good thing. Really.

924
00:36:39,030 --> 00:36:40,190
Now I know why

925
00:36:40,190 --> 00:36:41,440
they call you "Ms. Guo."

926
00:36:41,440 --> 00:36:42,370
You're a gossip.

927
00:36:43,780 --> 00:36:44,570
You kid.

928
00:36:44,600 --> 00:36:45,000
Zhang.

929
00:36:46,000 --> 00:36:46,920
I just went back to the mailroom

930
00:36:46,920 --> 00:36:48,150
and found a letter left behind.

931
00:36:48,150 --> 00:36:48,640
It's for you.

932
00:36:48,640 --> 00:36:49,350
Thank you.

933
00:36:49,370 --> 00:36:50,050
Sorry about that.

934
00:36:49,860 --> 00:36:51,870
[To Zhang Lihui; From Zheng Jianmin]

935
00:37:04,510 --> 00:37:06,440
Yours can't make long-distance calls,

936
00:37:06,440 --> 00:37:07,700
so you have to use mine.

937
00:37:09,590 --> 00:37:10,390
Right, right.

938
00:37:16,880 --> 00:37:17,480
Mentor.

939
00:37:19,070 --> 00:37:19,760
How did you know

940
00:37:19,760 --> 00:37:21,890
I needed to make a long-distance call?

941
00:37:21,920 --> 00:37:23,000
I know everything.

942
00:37:26,150 --> 00:37:26,480
Fine.

943
00:37:27,400 --> 00:37:29,400
Go ahead. I'll give you some privacy.

944
00:37:29,400 --> 00:37:30,260
No need. You...

945
00:37:30,550 --> 00:37:31,360
can stay.

946
00:37:33,030 --> 00:37:33,830
Alright then.

947
00:37:48,240 --> 00:37:49,800
See? I knew it.

948
00:37:50,070 --> 00:37:51,190
Alright, make the call.

949
00:37:51,190 --> 00:37:52,320
Go on. I'll step out.

950
00:38:05,960 --> 00:38:06,290
Okay.

951
00:38:06,840 --> 00:38:07,370
Jianmin!

952
00:38:08,000 --> 00:38:08,800
Phone for you.

953
00:38:15,030 --> 00:38:16,690
Hello, this is Zheng Jianmin.

954
00:38:17,150 --> 00:38:18,280
This is Zhang Lihui.

955
00:38:22,000 --> 00:38:22,440
Hello?

956
00:38:23,710 --> 00:38:25,590
Um... have you been well?

957
00:38:26,630 --> 00:38:27,490
I've been fine.

958
00:38:28,400 --> 00:38:29,980
I just received your letter.

959
00:38:29,980 --> 00:38:31,360
You asked for Yan Jicai's photos.

960
00:38:31,360 --> 00:38:32,760
What do you need them for?

961
00:38:34,110 --> 00:38:35,040
Hold on a moment.

962
00:39:08,550 --> 00:39:08,960
Hello?

963
00:39:10,920 --> 00:39:13,050
What's wrong? You sound out of breath.

964
00:39:13,710 --> 00:39:15,110
I ran over from my office.

965
00:39:15,280 --> 00:39:16,610
It's a bit of a distance.

966
00:39:19,000 --> 00:39:20,710
Next time, should I time you?

967
00:39:23,110 --> 00:39:23,920
Tell me,

968
00:39:24,230 --> 00:39:25,690
why do you need his photos?

969
00:39:26,070 --> 00:39:27,470
I'll explain that later.

970
00:39:28,150 --> 00:39:28,710
I need a few

971
00:39:28,710 --> 00:39:30,240
recent photos of Yan Jicai.

972
00:39:30,480 --> 00:39:31,510
Don't overexpose them.

973
00:39:31,510 --> 00:39:33,310
A little underexposure is fine.

974
00:39:33,800 --> 00:39:35,360
The point is for them to look as different

975
00:39:35,360 --> 00:39:36,190
as possible from his previous photos.

976
00:39:36,190 --> 00:39:38,230
The greater the contrast, the better.

977
00:39:38,230 --> 00:39:40,400
Are you trying to
use his current appearance

978
00:39:40,400 --> 00:39:42,130
to stir someone's conscience?

979
00:39:44,280 --> 00:39:45,810
Everyone has a conscience.

980
00:39:47,400 --> 00:39:47,880
Lihui,

981
00:39:48,840 --> 00:39:50,930
I've been a prosecutor for some years now.

982
00:39:50,930 --> 00:39:51,670
I've never seen anyone

983
00:39:51,670 --> 00:39:52,420
who deliberately wanted to

984
00:39:52,420 --> 00:39:54,480
turn a case into a wrongful conviction.

985
00:39:54,480 --> 00:39:56,080
You can believe in Yan Jicai,

986
00:39:56,400 --> 00:39:58,200
but you have to believe that too.

987
00:40:01,440 --> 00:40:01,840
Okay.

988
00:40:19,920 --> 00:40:21,550
Wang Danni, what's going on with you?

989
00:40:21,550 --> 00:40:22,680
Where's your focus?

990
00:40:23,120 --> 00:40:23,980
Did Lu Jianghan

991
00:40:24,000 --> 00:40:25,320
steal your soul away or something?

992
00:40:25,320 --> 00:40:26,360
Sorry, Coach Sun.

993
00:40:28,000 --> 00:40:29,200
All right, come down.

994
00:40:29,960 --> 00:40:30,670
Go watch from the side.

995
00:40:30,670 --> 00:40:31,390
Come on, Siyi.

996
00:40:31,390 --> 00:40:32,590
Demonstrate for her.

997
00:40:52,030 --> 00:40:54,190
Today's gymnastics moves are so hard.

998
00:40:54,320 --> 00:40:54,670
Yeah.

999
00:40:54,670 --> 00:40:55,800
I wonder if today...

1000
00:40:56,880 --> 00:40:57,480
Uncle Lyu!

1001
00:40:58,230 --> 00:41:00,110
Have you come to
disturb our training again?

1002
00:41:00,110 --> 00:41:00,670
No.

1003
00:41:00,920 --> 00:41:02,450
I'm just here to take a look.

1004
00:41:03,320 --> 00:41:04,510
Coach Sun is here.

1005
00:41:06,070 --> 00:41:06,750
Uncle Lyu.

1006
00:41:07,000 --> 00:41:09,130
This is practically a crime, you know.

1007
00:41:10,150 --> 00:41:11,670
Go. You two, go train.

1008
00:41:11,670 --> 00:41:13,670
That old man is pretty interesting.

1009
00:41:22,190 --> 00:41:22,720
Again.

1010
00:41:26,580 --> 00:41:27,740
Demonstrate for me?

1011
00:41:48,840 --> 00:41:49,770
Get back in line.

1012
00:41:54,960 --> 00:41:56,890
Let me stress this to you once more.

1013
00:41:57,070 --> 00:41:58,230
No matter how talented you are,

1014
00:41:58,230 --> 00:41:59,400
you still have to work hard!

1015
00:41:59,400 --> 00:42:00,360
Don't be silly.

1016
00:42:00,710 --> 00:42:01,670
With some things, in the end,

1017
00:42:01,670 --> 00:42:03,480
it's always the girls who lose out.

1018
00:42:03,480 --> 00:42:04,190
There are only a limited number of spots

1019
00:42:04,190 --> 00:42:06,000
in the provincial team selection.

1020
00:42:06,000 --> 00:42:07,200
If you don't want one,

1021
00:42:07,320 --> 00:42:08,450
plenty of others do!

1022
00:42:11,190 --> 00:42:12,650
Today's training is over.

1023
00:42:18,540 --> 00:42:20,140
You were the one who snitched

1024
00:42:20,190 --> 00:42:21,070
to Coach Sun

1025
00:42:21,070 --> 00:42:22,870
about Lu Jianghan and me, right?

1026
00:42:22,880 --> 00:42:24,080
You better watch out.

1027
00:42:24,840 --> 00:42:25,800
It wasn't me.

1028
00:42:27,150 --> 00:42:27,670
Siyi.

1029
00:42:29,280 --> 00:42:30,080
What's wrong?

1030
00:42:30,240 --> 00:42:31,360
The cafeteria is about to close,

1031
00:42:31,360 --> 00:42:32,920
and we still have training this afternoon.

1032
00:42:32,920 --> 00:42:34,380
Dad brought you some food.

1033
00:42:36,590 --> 00:42:37,510
Come on, Zheng!

1034
00:42:38,230 --> 00:42:38,880
Here you go!

1035
00:42:38,880 --> 00:42:40,760
Come on! Get him, get him!

1036
00:42:42,980 --> 00:42:44,920
Use your ultimate! Use your ultimate!

1037
00:42:44,920 --> 00:42:47,110
Get him! Get him!

1038
00:42:48,150 --> 00:42:49,360
Get him! Get him!

1039
00:42:50,720 --> 00:42:51,680
Give me a chance!

1040
00:42:51,710 --> 00:42:52,880
Use your ultimate!

1041
00:42:55,320 --> 00:42:55,760
You...

1042
00:42:56,650 --> 00:42:57,090
I won.

1043
00:42:57,320 --> 00:42:58,960
No, don't fight if you're stunned.

1044
00:42:58,960 --> 00:43:00,030
Give me a chance.

1045
00:43:00,230 --> 00:43:01,590
You've only been practicing
for a few days,

1046
00:43:01,590 --> 00:43:03,110
yet you can already last 3 rounds with me.
